; TEST: abort=1 c-emit-exit=4
;
; `rem i64 -9223372036854775808 -1`: the T_MIN / -1 trap for `rem`, at
; width 64, where T_MIN really is INT64_MIN.
;
; TWO THINGS ONLY THIS FIXTURE PINS.
;
; 1. `rem` TRAPS HERE, where its mathematical value is 0 -- a perfectly good
;    `i64`. The decision (spec 5.4, 2026-09-25) is that `rem` is the
;    remainder OF THE TRUNCATING DIVISION, so where the division does not
;    exist neither does its remainder; and a `rem` answering 0 where its
;    `div` traps would break `a == (a/b)*b + (a rem b)` at exactly the one
;    pair of operands where both halves are checkable. Nothing in the
;    RESULT could carry this: the check has to precede the divide, and this
;    fixture is what says so.
; 2. AT WIDTH 64 THE CHECK ALSO REPLACES A HARDWARE FAULT. `idiv` on
;    INT64_MIN / -1 raises #DE -- SIGFPE, signal 8 -- and this tree's
;    numeric trap is SIGILL with `abortus 1`. The harness compares the
;    SIGNAL, so a lowering that let the hardware do the trapping fails here
;    rather than passing by accident.
;
; If nothing traps the function returns 7.
;
; Mutation (run): the T_MIN / -1 check emitted for `div` only -> signal 8
; (SIGFPE) instead of SIGILL. The same check removed at width 64 on the
; theory that the hardware covers it -> the same signal 8.
;
; `c-emit-exit=4`: the C backend refuses `rem` by name (c-backend.md D4
; row 5).

functio @initium (ptr) -> u8 {
b0:
%0 = param ptr 0
%1 = iconst i64 -9223372036854775808
%2 = iconst i64 -1
%3 = rem i64 %1 %2
%4 = iconst u8 7
ret %4
}
